  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TA for Rite Water Solutions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rite Water is seeking Technical Assistance (TA) to facilitate the completion of all necessary tasks for registering its Programme of Activities (&quot;PoA&quot;) linked to Electro-chlorination Systems (EC) for the Voluntary Carbon Market Programme (&quot;VCM&quot;). This registration will enable the company to generate carbon credits for its activities. Registering it&#x2019;s PoA under the &quot;Gold Standard&quot; would mark a significant milestone, certifying EC as a climate mitigation project for the first time on the VCM. A high level calculation of the preferred service provider Kosher climate estimated the possible revenue coming from carbon credits to be around USD 12,000,000 over the course of 5 to 10 years. The revenue would provide an additional income stream to support the maintenance and operation of the EC systems in the long term.</narrative>
  </description>
